    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11439" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coxa</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the hip</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop, <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
				22, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 1</span></i>
			<i>fin.</i>; 8, 10, 5; <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Tard. 4, 3, 38</span></i>; cf. also
			coxendix.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The hip-bone</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 2,
				1, 5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>,  in the Agrimensores:
			agrorum, <i>a bend inwards</i> (with angulus), Sic.
			Fl. p. 6 Goes.</div>
